==Trivia==
*The Boss Bandit may be inspired by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robin_Hood Robin Hood], an English outlaw known from robbing from wealthy families and distributing that wealth to poorer ones.
*The word "''Bandit''" comes from the Latin "''bannio''", meaning 'to ban'.
**The Boss Bandit is 1 of 4 [[cards]] associated with outlawry, with the others being [[Goblin Gang]], [[Rascals]], and [[Bandit]].
**Along with the [[Firecracker]], Rascals, [[Magic Archer]], and Bandit, the Boss Bandit belongs to the Forest Gang.
**In the Turkish language setting of the game, the word "Boss" is not translated, making Boss Bandit the only card with a word from an foreign language in the Turkish language setting.
*The Boss Bandit is the most expensive {{Rarity|Champion}} card, costing 6 [[Elixir]].
**Along with the [[Golden Knight]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Monk]], and the [[Terry]], she also has the cheapest ability cost, costing 1 Elixir.
**Also along with the [[Goblinstein]], she also has the most expensive combined Elixir cost of '''{{Rarity|Champion}}''' and ability, costing 7 Elixir.
*The Boss Bandit is the first {{Rarity|Champion}} to have a limited number of ability uses, with a maximum of two uses per deployment.
*If the Boss Bandit's ability is used up, the crown symbol is currently not automatically removed. 
*Upon deployment, the Boss Bandit exclaims "''In and out, just like that!''", "''Let's make this quick.''", or "''Let's steal the show!''". When attacking a troop, she may say "''Hey! Knife to meet you!''", or "''The crown is calling me''". When Getaway Grenade is activated, she may say "''Catch me if you can!''", "''Too slow!''", "''You lost me!''", "''Eyes on me!''", or "''Lost me again!''". She will also whistle before dashing, and may say "''Hah! Now you see me!''". When idle or attacking, she may say "''You wanna win the crown for me? Really?''".
**The Boss Bandit is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Bowler]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Electro Wizard]], [[Princess]], [[Ice Wizard]], Magic Archer, [[Lumberjack]], [[Mother Witch]], [[Fisherman]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Little Prince]], and the [[Terry]].
**The Boss Bandit has unique lines that only play on specific occasions, which override her normal lines:
***If the Boss Bandit takes down an opposing Bandit, she may say "''This is why I'm the boss!''". If the Boss Bandit is taken down by an opposing Bandit, she may say "''Beaten by you?''" If the Boss Bandit is played when an allied Bandit is on the field, she says "''Bandit, watch and learn!''".
***If the Boss Bandit is played when an allied Firecracker is on the field, she says "''You fire, I dash!''".
***If the Boss Bandit is played when an allied Magic Archer is on the field, she says "''Cover me, sharp eyes!''".
***If the Boss Bandit is played when allied Rascals are on the field, she says "''Trouble squad, I'm in!''".
***If the Boss Bandit is played when 2 or more allied Forest Gang members are on the field, she says "''Forest Gang, roll out!''" or "''Troublemakers, party time!''".

* The Boss Bandit is 1 of 10 cards to have an alliterative name, the others being the [[Royal Recruits]], Goblin Gang, Mega Minion, [[Goblin Giant]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], Ram Rider, [[Dagger Duchess]], and the Mighty Miner.
* The Boss Bandit is the subject of a few cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Boss Bandit is the subject of 3 [[Emotes]].
**The Boss Bandit is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] Decorations, including an animated one.
*The initial balance change for Boss Bandit on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/7/2025)|8/7/2025 balance changes]] was an addition of a 5-second cooldown to Getaway Grenade, but it was lowered to 3 seconds [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-73-balance-wip-july-2025 last minute].

